---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../config';
---

<BaseLayout title="How We Review" description={`How ${SITE.name} researches and writes its gear reviews.`}>
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>How We Review</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Every review tells you up front how it was written: hands-on testing, research, or both.
    </p>

    <h2>Do we test every product ourselves?</h2>
    <p>
      Not always. When we've used a product in the studio, we say so. When we haven't, the review clearly states
      that it's based on research, so you know exactly what you're reading.
    </p>

    <h2>What sources do we use?</h2>
    <p>
      We start with the manufacturer's official specs and documentation. We then read owner reviews on Amazon and
      look for patterns: what people consistently love, and what they consistently complain about.
    </p>

    <h2>How do we keep owner sentiment fair?</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>We read reviews from every star rating on purpose, so critical opinions are well represented.</li>
      <li>We only count reviews of the exact model, not older or different versions.</li>
      <li>We tell you how many reviews we read, and we note when a point comes from only one or two owners.</li>
      <li>We summarize in our own words and never copy review text.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Do affiliate links influence our verdicts?</h2>
    <p>
      No. We earn a commission on some purchases (see our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>),
      but we include the downsides and common complaints for every product, and we never show prices that go out of
      date.
    </p>

    <h2>What if something is wrong or out of date?</h2>
    <p>Please <a href="/contact/">tell us</a>. We update reviews and show the updated date at the top of each post.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
